{
  "question_id": "q_095_first_month_retention",
  "slug": "first-month-retention",
  "title": "First Month Retention",
  "difficulty": "Hard",
  "company": "Facebook",
  "premium": true,
  "question": "Mobile gaming product managers track player retention to see how many new players keep playing after their install month.\n\nA player's **install month** is the calendar month of their `signup_date` in `users`. A player is **retained in month 1** if `user_actions` contains at least one `'login'` action for them during the calendar month immediately after their install month (other action types such as `'post'` do not count).\n\nWrite a query to calculate, for each install month, the percentage of players who were retained in month 1, rounded to 2 decimal places. Output `install_month` (formatted `'YYYY-MM'`) and `retention_pct`, sorted by `install_month`.",
  "notes": [
    "June cohort: users 1, 2 and 3 signed up. Users 1 and 3 logged in during July, user 2 only posted, so 2 of 3 = 66.67%.",
    "July cohort: user 4 logged in during August, so 100.00%."
  ],
  "tables": [
    {
      "table_name": "users",
      "columns": [
        {
          "column_name": "user_id",
          "data_type": "INT"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "signup_date",
          "data_type": "DATETIME"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "table_name": "user_actions",
      "columns": [
        {
          "column_name": "user_id",
          "data_type": "INT"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "event_date",
          "data_type": "DATETIME"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "action_type",
          "data_type": "VARCHAR(255)"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "sample_data": {
    "users": [
      {
        "user_id": 1,
        "signup_date": "06/01/2022 00:00:00"
      },
      {
        "user_id": 2,
        "signup_date": "06/02/2022 00:00:00"
      },
      {
        "user_id": 3,
        "signup_date": "06/08/2022 00:00:00"
      },
      {
        "user_id": 4,
        "signup_date": "07/03/2022 00:00:00"
      }
    ],
    "user_actions": [
      {
        "user_id": 1,
        "event_date": "06/10/2022 00:00:00",
        "action_type": "login"
      },
      {
        "user_id": 1,
        "event_date": "07/10/2022 00:00:00",
        "action_type": "login"
      },
      {
        "user_id": 2,
        "event_date": "07/15/2022 00:00:00",
        "action_type": "post"
      },
      {
        "user_id": 3,
        "event_date": "06/12/2022 00:00:00",
        "action_type": "login"
      },
      {
        "user_id": 3,
        "event_date": "07/20/2022 00:00:00",
        "action_type": "login"
      },
      {
        "user_id": 4,
        "event_date": "08/05/2022 00:00:00",
        "action_type": "login"
      }
    ]
  },
  "sample_output": [
    {
      "install_month": "2022-06",
      "retention_pct": 66.67
    },
    {
      "install_month": "2022-07",
      "retention_pct": 100
    }
  ],
  "reference_sql": "SELECT\n  DATE_FORMAT(u.signup_date, '%Y-%m') AS install_month,\n  ROUND(100.0 * COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN a.user_id IS NOT NULL THEN u.user_id END)\n        / COUNT(DISTINCT u.user_id), 2) AS retention_pct\nFROM users u\nLEFT JOIN user_actions a\n  ON a.user_id = u.user_id\n AND a.action_type = 'login'\n AND DATE_FORMAT(a.event_date, '%Y-%m') = DATE_FORMAT(DATE_ADD(u.signup_date, INTERVAL 1 MONTH), '%Y-%m')\nGROUP BY DATE_FORMAT(u.signup_date, '%Y-%m')\nORDER BY install_month;",
  "tags": [
    "date-manipulation",
    "facebook",
    "hard",
    "math",
    "social-media"
  ],
